The order some events take place seems a little strange, have you
noticed how if you walk into a pit while blind you feel the items
on the ground and THEN you fall into the pit ?
Also weak pets can jump into a  pit  after  a  corpse, eat it and
then die from the trap dammage !
Blessed rings of poly control could give a message like "You feel
unstable, return to human form?" instead of  automatically  going
back to your normal self when a poly wears off. For all those out
there (like me) who would quite fancy finishing  the  game  as  a
Master Lich or Vampire Lord.
Chaotic characters should not get the  same  penalty  for  eating
human/elf corpses as Neutrals and Lawfuls do.
To balance this, chaotics could be charged more by shops / oracle
as chaotics are notorius for stealing etc.
Have you noticed that with str 25 you cant pick up  boulders  but
with any sort of Giant form you can?
Have you noticed that you  can  fall  through  a  trapdoor  while
carrying 10 boulders but just 1 boulder will plug a trapdoor?
On a similar note it would be nice to be able  to  push  boulders
down stairs.
Id also like to be able to slowly drag objects along even if they
are too heavy to actually lift.
How about allowing the disarming of  standard ^  traps,  although
with a much reduced chance and, of course, failure would  usually
result in setting off the trap.
And you could have thief type monsters that  go  around  creating
the occaisional random trap, will never step  into  a  trap,  and
has stealing & backstab attacks (maybe hide in  shads  like  rock
piercers some of the time).
And you could even have a plumber that creates a sink on top of a
fountain :)
(Getting carried away now)
Dont you think that digging down from a fountain should create  a
water pool?
And there could be a (very small)  chance  of  breaking  into  an
underground stream when digging a pit.
(Some very pedantic stuff)
While under water with a amulet of magical breathing I cant  seem
to be able to quaff the water.
Ive never seen a lava pool but if you have  fire  resistance  and
magical breathing can you survive them?  And  can  you  dip  your
stuff in them? (Your long sword glows a cheery red -  double  dam
against non fire res monsters for a while)
